'''Cannot die aura''' is a [[monster aura]]. Player has to kite the monster with the aura away from other monsters, or kill the monster with the aura directly, in order to kill the monster pack.

The aura effect displays the [[descry]] symbol. The symbol represents [[Innocence (NPC)|Innocence]] or the [[Order of the Templar|Templar]] faction of in-game world.

Since [[version 3.14.0]] the aura is largely removed from the game, but with exceptions such as [[Vaal Totem]]s.<ref name="cannotdie314"/> 

Note that the aura is different from [[Maker of Mires]]' aura/buff. Monsters that have "others cannot die aura" can be slayed, while Maker of Mires's buff makes it invulnerable but does not grant invulnerability to its allies.

==Sources==
Any monster with the modifier [[Modifier:MonsterImplicitAuraCannotDie1|MonsterImplicitAuraCannotDie1]], [[Modifier:MonsterImplicitAuraCannotDie2|MonsterImplicitAuraCannotDie2]] (unique modifiers for unique monsters and vaal totems), for example:
* [[Titan of the Grove]], a map boss ([[Gneiss]], the act variant does not have this mod)
* [[Grath]], an invasion boss
* [[Mother of the Hive]], a Vaal side area boss
* [[Vaal Totem]]s (despite displayed as normal rarity, it cannot be raised as [[spectre]])

The mod [[Modifier:MonsterAuraCannotDie1|MonsterAuraCannotDie1]] (prefix) no longer spawns after 3.14, despite it may be found in permanent leagues' [[The Menagerie]] or itemized beast, which monsters with this mod are captured by the players before the mod's removal.

==Version history==
The monster with this aura was used to have this text under their monster nameplate: "{{c|normal|Other Allies Cannot Die}}". It is removed due to introduction of archnemesis modifier to core game and subsequent reworks.

Cannot die aura (except totem) was replaced by {{c|nemesis|Benevolent Guardian}} which behave differently. Although that nemesis mod is replaced again in [[version 3.18.0]] by [[archnemesis]] monster mod Invulnerable, which is more resembled to the behaviour of Cannot die aura. This change was revoked again in [[version 3.18.0c]] to make "Invulnerable" mod behave like {{c|nemesis|Benevolent Guardian}}. After a generally negative review on most archnemssis mod among the players community, [[Version 3.20.0]] removed archnemesis mod from the monster and replaced by new set of mods, however, the mod {{ml|MonsterModBenevolentGuardian}} ({{c|normal|Invulnerability Aura}}) is still somewhat resemble to {{c|nemesis|Benevolent Guardian}}.
